.TH XL-SCREENSHOT 1 "November 2026" "xl-Screenshot 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xl-screenshot \- take a screenshot of the screen, a window, or a selection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xl-screenshot
[\-\-selection] [\-\-tray] [\-\-version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xl-Screenshot
captures the whole screen, a single window (with its titlebar), or an area drawn over a still
picture of the desktop. A delay can be set before the capture; Esc cancels it. The capture can be
copied, saved as PNG, JPEG, or WebP, or marked up in
.BR xl-annotate (1).
.PP
Only one copy runs at a time: starting it again brings up the window that is already open.
.PP
With "Show in System Tray" turned on in its menu, clicking the tray icon starts a Selection
capture, closing the window only hides it, and xl-Screenshot starts at login.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-selection
Start a Selection capture right away. If xl-Screenshot is already running, the running copy
starts it. Useful for a keyboard shortcut.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tray
Start with just the tray icon (what the login entry uses).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/xl-screenshot/config.json
The save format, delay, last save folder, and other settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.xlcheese.XlScreenshot.desktop
Starts xl-Screenshot at login; present only while the tray icon is turned on.
.SH AUTHOR
Wesley Hayslip.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xl-annotate (1),
https://github.com/xlcheese/xl-screenshot
